Epistemic hubris is a fascinating concept that refers to a particular kind of intellectual overconfidence - specifically, when someone's expertise in one domain leads them to overestimate their ability to understand or solve problems in other domains.

For example:
============
A successful physicist might believe they can easily solve economic problems because they're good at mathematical modeling

A prominent tech entrepreneur might think they can solve complex social issues because they've built successful companies

A celebrated doctor might assume they understand climate science because they're well-versed in scientific methodology

